    "## Downtown Dublin Is Getting Attention",
    "While industrial development is bringing investment to the area, Dublin has also been working to improve its historic downtown.",
    "The Madison Street Redevelopment Project is among the most visible examples.",
    "The approximately $4.6 million project covers three blocks between Church Street and Jefferson Street. Improvements include wider pedestrian areas, landscaping, traffic-calming measures and streetscape upgrades intended to make the district more accessible and inviting.",
    "State funding helped support the work.",
    "The improvements are also part of a longer-term effort to strengthen connections between downtown and the Oconee River.",
    "Dublin has retained several historic landmarks that continue to serve the public.",
    "The Carnegie Library, built in the early twentieth century, has been preserved and adapted for community use. Theatre Dublin, another prominent downtown landmark, continues to contribute to the city's cultural life.",
    "These buildings give downtown a character that newer commercial developments cannot easily reproduce.",
