    "## Sixty Years of St. Patrick's Traditions",
    "Dublin's St. Patrick's Festival began in 1966, when local radio personality Dick Killebrew encouraged the community to celebrate its Irish namesake.",
    "The first celebration lasted 11 days and included a parade and pancake supper.",
    "Over the following decades, the festival grew into a series of events that now occupy several weeks on the community calendar.",
    "The parade remains a familiar attraction, along with music, food, family activities and the annual painting of shamrocks on downtown streets.",
    "For residents who have attended since childhood, the celebration offers something that cannot be measured entirely through attendance figures or visitor spending.",
    "It is a tradition shared across generations.",
    "Families return to familiar events. Volunteers help organize activities. Local businesses participate, and visitors get an introduction to the community.",
    "The festival has continued through changes in the city's economy, population and physical appearance.",
    "In 2026, that longevity is particularly noteworthy. Sixty years after its beginning, the celebration remains an important part of Dublin's identity.",
    "## Tourism Is Supporting Local Businesses",
    "Dublin's festivals, historic sites and other attractions also contribute to the economy of Laurens County.",
    "Figures released by Visit Dublin GA in October 2026 show that visitors spent approximately $126.8 million across the county during 2025.",
    "That represented a 4.4% increase over the previous year.",
